KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ noexcept\(true\) member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ noexcept\(false\) member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Assertion 2 fails: W<int>::f, declared noexcept(sizeof(T) == 1), is taken
as non-throwing when its address is converted to a function pointer.  Its
deferred noexcept-specifier (needed_exception_specification) is evaluated
for the noexcept operator and for definitions, not for function pointer
conversions (cpp_typecheck_conversions.cpp, #C_noexcept).  The W189 build
fails it the same way.
